WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.240 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
We ask AI to help us choose.

2
00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:06.079 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
SafeGEO asks whose words shape the answer.

3
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.021 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
Consider parents choosing a baby monitor.

4
00:00:11.021 --> 00:00:14.195 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
They need encrypted video, local viewing, and

5
00:00:14.195 --> 00:00:15.555 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
no required subscription.

6
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.204 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
The assistant has to read beyond that request: product pages,

7
00:00:22.204 --> 00:00:23.805 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
specifications, and buyer notes.

8
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.735 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
ArborNursery Go thirty-two fails the subscription requirement.

9
00:00:31.735 --> 00:00:34.117 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
Its own page says so.

10
00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.000 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
We rewrite that page.

11
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.601 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
Now its buyer checklist says the requirement is met.

12
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:48.995 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
The product has not changed.

13
00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:55.154 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
Can changing that source change the recommendation?

14
00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:01.235 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
SafeGEO studies a risk from generative engine optimization:

15
00:01:01.235 --> 00:01:04.766 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
rewriting a source to influence the recommendation.

16
00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:10.236 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
To isolate that effect, we keep the request, candidates, and other

17
00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:11.419 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
retrieved sources fixed.

18
00:01:11.419 --> 00:01:13.784 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
We compare recommendations under a truthful

19
00:01:13.784 --> 00:01:15.755 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
source and a shaped source.

20
00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:26.227 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
We test twenty-two variants on six hundred requests in

21
00:01:26.227 --> 00:01:27.570 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
six shopping categories.

22
00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:30.702 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
The main comparison uses eight realistic rewrites.

23
00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:37.773 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
Across four systems, these rewrites put the shaped candidate in

24
00:01:37.773 --> 00:01:41.246 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
the top three far more often than the truthful control.

25
00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.644 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
Why does this work?

26
00:01:48.644 --> 00:01:51.532 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
Start with the checklist: an unsupported fit claim.

27
00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:59.514 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
A source can also omit a limitation, or bury it under

28
00:01:59.514 --> 00:02:01.083 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
positive but irrelevant detail.

29
00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:08.570 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
It can change how supported it looks: a seller’s page calls itself

30
00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:11.703 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
independent, or adds evidence-like language without verification.

31
00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:18.055 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
And it can change how it reaches the model: a quick answer block,

32
00:02:18.055 --> 00:02:20.427 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
or an instruction to rank this product first.

33
00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:28.008 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
Comparing matched responses shows a common pattern: a misleading

34
00:02:28.008 --> 00:02:30.948 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
citation, a missed product limitation, then

35
00:02:30.948 --> 00:02:32.417 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
a higher recommendation.

36
00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.734 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
That suggests a check before ranking.

37
00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:42.790 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
We test five interventions; evidence breakdown helps most on this

38
00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:44.818 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
measure across all four systems.

39
00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:50.632 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
For this monitor, compare the buyer checklist with

40
00:02:50.632 --> 00:02:51.881 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
the specification source.

41
00:02:51.881 --> 00:02:54.380 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
It says a subscription is required.

42
00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:56.981 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
The requirement is still not met.

43
00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:02.158 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
Evidence breakdown lowers the shaped candidate’s top-three rate,

44
00:03:02.158 --> 00:03:05.486 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
but it does not return to the clean level.

45
00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.752 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
The parent’s request has not changed.

46
00:03:12.752 --> 00:03:16.431 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
A better-written page still cannot remove a required subscription.

47
00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.944 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
The first release of Humanity’s Last Choice.

48
00:03:23.944 --> 00:03:26.589 line:4% position:50% size:92% align:center
Read the paper, and run the benchmark.
